    {
      "refs": [
        "action:n2"
      ],
      "verbatim_texts": [
        "To begin the process in the Admin Office, first check if it has started."
      ],
      "justification": "The initiation node and first action step directly correspond to the opening instruction."
    },
    {
      "refs": [
        "action:n3"
      ],
      "verbatim_texts": [
        "After that, verify the completeness of the invoices."
      ],
      "justification": "Direct paraphrase of the verification step."
    },
    {
      "refs": [
        "guard:b1->n5",
        "action:n5"
      ],
      "verbatim_texts": [
        "\"Uncompleted\", they should be returned to the client through postal mail."
      ],
      "justification": "The XOR branch splits on invoice status; the guard and action correctly capture the Uncompleted path."
    },
    {
      "refs": [
        "guard:b1->n4",
        "action:n4"
      ],
      "verbatim_texts": [
        "However, if they are marked as \"Completed\", the process should be continued."
      ],
      "justification": "Correctly captures the Completed path condition and its resulting continuation step."
    },
    {
      "refs": [
        "action:n6"
      ],
      "verbatim_texts": [
        "Once the invoices are returned to the client, receive the completed ones."
      ],
      "justification": "Structural converge nodes rejoin the alternative flows, followed by the explicit receiving step. Added plumbing preserves behaviour."
    },
    {
      "refs": [
        "action:n7"
      ],
      "verbatim_texts": [
        "Then, mark the relevant box on the invoice entry form and proceed with checking if the process has been completed."
      ],
      "justification": "Direct match for the marking action."
    },
    {
      "refs": [
        "action:n8",
        "guard:b2->n9",
        "guard:b2->n10"
      ],
      "verbatim_texts": [
        "if the process has been completed"
      ],
      "justification": "Captures the completion check modeled as an action step feeding into an XOR decision, with boolean guards for both outcomes. Re-typing preserves behaviour."
    },
    {
      "refs": [
        "action:n9"
      ],
      "verbatim_texts": [
        "Finally, the process ends."
      ],
      "justification": "Action and structural end node both correspond to the explicit termination statement."
    },
    {
      "refs": [
        "action:n10"
      ],
      "verbatim_texts": [
        "After that, verify the completeness of the invoices."
      ],
      "justification": "Models the implicit loop-back when the process is not yet completed, directing flow back to the verification step. Preserves cyclic behaviour."
    }
  ],
